diff --git a/xz1c-engine/README.md b/xz1c-engine/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..3c5ff8b0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xz1c-engine/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# XZ1C configurable encrypted DNS engine
+
+Protocols: DoT (TLS), DoH (HTTP/2), DoH3 (HTTP/3), DoQ (RFC 9250).
+Servers are configurable; AliDNS is only the initial field value, not a restriction.
+The Settings dialog persists xz1c_dns_protocol and xz1c_dns_endpoint alongside the
+standard strict private DNS hostname. Connectivity passes a project-local xz1c:
+hint in DohParamsParcel.dohpath; this hint is consumed locally, never transmitted.
+The parcel interface remains frozen and compatible with unmodified callers.
+
+Every upstream socket inherits Android's app_mark for that network and is tagged
+with AID_DNS. It does not use a global default route or a hostname lookup in Go.
+Android performs the resolver-hostname bootstrap on the corresponding network.
+That initial hostname bootstrap may use that network's DNS. These settings do not
+force independently implemented application DNS, excluded VPN apps, connectivity
+probes or split routes into a tunnel. VPN lockdown and on-device traffic capture
+are separate requirements for verifying traffic stays inside a WireGuard tunnel.
+
+The selected transport never falls back to plaintext or another transport.
+System trust roots and the configured hostname are verified. DoH redirects are
+rejected. DNS response IDs, questions and record framing are checked before use.
+DoQ uses DNS message ID zero on the wire and restores the application ID locally.
+Connections are pooled per network configuration; deletion cancels queries and
+closes sockets. Configuration changes replace the old pool.
+
+## Rebuild and verification
+
+Pinned toolchain: Go 1.26.0. Transport dependency: quic-go v0.63.0 (MIT).
+Dependencies are vendored with their licenses. build-android.sh rebuilds the
+arm64/arm Android shared libraries using the tree's Clang and generated NDK
+sysroot. Source/engine changes require rebuilding these libraries first.
+
+Host tests: go test -mod=vendor -race ./...
+Live AliDNS tests: XZ1C_DNS_LIVE=1 go test -mod=vendor -v -run TestAliDNSLive ./...
+Project modules: /home/joey/build.sh codex-dns "Settings com.android.resolv com.android.tethering"
+
+The legacy resolver statistics schema has no distinct DoQ protocol enum; custom
+engine events use its encrypted transport envelope. dumpsys dnsresolver identifies
+the actual chosen protocol and port. Build checks and host endpoint tests do not
+prove phone boot, SELinux behavior, or VPN routing; those need physical-device tests.
+Use the project's signed release entry point for installable system updates.
